A Looker developer is adding a measure to a view that should count the number of unique order IDs placed by each customer. They write the following LookML block:

```yaml
view: orders {
  sql_table_name: sales.orders ;;

  measure: unique_orders {
    type: count
    sql: ${TABLE}.order_id ;;
    label: "Unique Orders"
    description: "Number of distinct orders placed"
    value_format_name: decimal_0
  }
}
```

Which parameter in the `unique_orders` measure block is incorrect for counting unique order IDs?

A data engineer creates an Eventarc trigger intended to invoke a Cloud Run service whenever a CSV file is finalized in a Cloud Storage bucket. The trigger is created with the following configuration:

```json
{
  "name": "projects/my-project/locations/us-central1/triggers/csv-ingest-trigger",
  "serviceAccount": "pipeline-sa@my-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com",
  "eventFilters": [
    {
      "attribute": "type",
      "value": "google.cloud.storage.object.v1.finalized"
    },
    {
      "attribute": "bucket",
      "value": "my-landing-bucket"
    },
    {
      "attribute": "suffix",
      "value": ".csv"
    }
  ],
  "destination": {
    "cloudRun": {
      "service": "csv-processor",
      "path": "/ingest"
    }
  }
}
```

After deploying, the Cloud Run service is never triggered when CSV files are uploaded. Which field in the configuration is the cause?

A storage administrator wants to configure a Cloud Storage bucket so that objects are automatically deleted 90 days after creation. They apply the following lifecycle configuration to the bucket:

```json
{
  "lifecycle": {
    "rule": [
      {
        "action": {
          "type": "SetStorageClass",
          "storageClass": "NEARLINE"
        },
        "condition": {
          "age": 90
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

After 90 days, objects are moved to Nearline storage instead of being deleted. Which field value must be changed to achieve the intended behavior?

A security architect reviews a BigQuery table resource configuration that includes the following `encryptionConfiguration` block:

```json
{
  "kind": "bigquery#table",
  "tableReference": {
    "projectId": "my-project",
    "datasetId": "analytics",
    "tableId": "user_events"
  },
  "schema": {
    "fields": [
      { "name": "user_id",    "type": "STRING" },
      { "name": "event_type", "type": "STRING" },
      { "name": "event_ts",   "type": "TIMESTAMP" }
    ]
  },
  "encryptionConfiguration": {
    "kmsKeyName": "projects/my-project/locations/us-central1/keyRings/my-ring/cryptoKeys/my-key"
  }
}
```

What does the `encryptionConfiguration` block protect, and what does it NOT protect?
